---
import { TRIAL_DAYS } from '../business'
import Support from '../components/Support.astro'
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
---
<Legal
  title="Refund and cancellation policy"
  description="How to cancel a Stoke plan, and when you can get a refund."
  updated="October 16, 2026"
>
  <h2>Cancelling</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Paid plans start with a {TRIAL_DAYS}-day free trial. Cancel before it ends and you’re never charged.</li>
    <li>You can cancel your plan at any time in Stoke, or by emailing <Support />.</li>
    <li>Your plan stays active until the end of the billing period you’ve already paid for. It isn’t renewed, and you aren’t charged again.</li>
    <li>There are no cancellation fees.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Every paid plan starts with a {TRIAL_DAYS}-day free trial, so you can try everything before you pay. Because of
      that, payments aren’t refunded, including for partial periods. Cancelling stops all future charges.
    </li>
    <li>If we charge you in error, or Stoke is unavailable for a long stretch through our fault, we’ll refund the affected period.</li>
    <li>Refunds go back to the card you paid with, and usually show up within 5–10 business days, depending on your bank.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Changing plans</h2>
  <p>
    Upgrades take effect straight away, and you pay the difference for the rest of the period. Downgrades take effect
    at the next renewal.
  </p>
  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Deleting your account in Settings also cancels your plan. It doesn’t refund the current period.
  </p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <Support />.</p>
</Legal>
